hellraiser's iconic pinhead is a  touchstone of cinematic horror  but he didn't begin that way in fact  he's not even called pinhead until the  third movie  it took multiple movies to make the hell  priest into the monster we know and love  this is his story in its gruesome  entirety  so what is pinhead while he's presented  as a simple extra dimensional pain  monster in the original hellraiser  later movies in the series dive into  pinhead's backstory revealing that he  was once a british soldier  named elliot spencer who served in world  war one  pinhead's human origins are first  indicated in the second film  hellbound when an old photograph forces  pinhead to remember his former life  prior to his time in the hell dimension  the monster was just a man who took up  arms in service to his country  only to have his faith and humanity  shaken during the battle of flanders  doug bradley who played pinhead in most  of the hellraiser films  once explained how spencer went from a  charismatic leader of men  to someone seeking out the kind of pain  doled out by the cenobites  in the dvd commentary for hellraiser 3  hell on earth bradley recalled watching  a war documentary and being influenced  by it  saying one of the guys said this  extraordinary thing i just grabbed hold  of  talking about all his comrades who had  died on the first day of the battle of  the psalm  he felt as though he had cheated that he  was in the wrong place that he shouldn't  have lived that he should be dead and  he should have been buried along with  his comrades and friends  and i thought that's exactly elliot's  thing  trying to deal with the trauma of war  sends elliot spencer down a path  that leads him to some pretty dark  places  the first thing you need to know about  pinhead is that he's a cenobite  these types of creatures live in another  dimension and are characterized by their  extensive mutilation  and obsession with pain and ritual  torture anyone  unlucky enough to come in contact with  them and their hell dimension  is subject to any number of outlandish  punishments  almost all of the cenobytes were humans  before being transported into the hell  dimension by opening a cursed puzzle box  and these unlucky souls become servants  of leviathan  pinhead specific group is known as the  order of the gash which is  kind of a religious sect we learn in  hellraiser two and three  that eliot spencer himself was drawn to  the box that serves as a key to the hell  dimension while testing his limits for  pain  the first scene of this series shows a  similarly adventurous frank cotton  being torn to shreds by meat hooks after  discovering the box on a trip to morocco  of course frank makes an attempt to come  back to our world while spencer becomes  pinhead  and gets quite cozy as the leader of the  order of the gash  the backstory of the box that leads to  pinhead's world is nearly as detailed as  the creature's own origin  the lament configuration is a puzzle box  created by  architect mass murderer and all-around  pervert  philip le marshall in the hellraiser  comics when he wasn't creating intricate  cathedrals or  killing indiscriminately the french  artisan would build puzzle boxes meant  to reveal deeply held secrets or  satisfying dark desires  for anyone who could solve them in the  movies however  le marchan is just a toy maker the  lament configuration is just one such  box created while limaushan was working  as a toymaker  he made the box for a rich duke with a  penchant for murder  and an extreme interest in occult  practices  solving the box sets the cenobites free  to enact their elaborate tortures and  probably drag you to hell too  where you'll be flayed into another  grotesque monster  pinhead's story grows far more fleshed  out in hellraiser 3  which spends much of its time exploring  human misery and war  naturally pinhead shares how he felt as  a human soldier  watching so many of his fellow  countrymen perish on the front lines  pinhead as eliot spencer plainly states  that his disrupted faith in people and  god after the war  led him to experiment with torture pain  to pinhead is truth and everything else  is noise the degradation of war is the  final discovery the end point of  civilization  the only thing in a world full of  falsehoods  everyone will figure it out in the end  he just got there a little faster  the story of what pinhead actually is  can get a little muddled  the first two films show him as a  nameless demon then a former human on a  quest to inflict pain  which he sees as necessary during that  second film however  elliott spencer's spirit is trapped in  limbo what's left behind  without spencer's humanity is a  completely evil pinhead  at least until the end of the third  movie but there's an alternate story  presented by the 1993 pinhead comic  miniseries  which claims that pinhead is just the  latest reincarnation of an ancient aztec  deity  zypa totec while zypatotek was an  agricultural god associated with the  regular rebirth of seasons  he also ritually flayed himself to feed  humanity sometimes even peeling off his  skin entirely to reveal a golden body  underneath  his followers believed that totec  invented the concept of war and desired  human sacrifices  much the way the cenobites constantly  need new humans to torture  hellraiser creator clive barker himself  has made the religious elements of  pinhead's story explicit  if naming their dimension hell and  having pinhead deliver a treatise  against god wasn't enough  several of the movies refer to him as a  priest or even a pope  i am the way  pinhead himself is a little more humble  about the whole thing calling himself  an explorer in the further regions of  experience  he does admit however to encouraging  holy connotations and says that  depending on temperament  people view the cenobites as either  angels or demons  if barker had his way the character  would be known as a leader of hell  first and a guy with pins sticking out  of his face last  saying in an interview in my original  script pinhead didn't even have a name  pinhead was the name that the special  effects guy used actually i was like  wait a second you just named my villain  pinhead because i didn't think that  sounded very dignified  but it ended up on the call sheet and it  just stuck  pinhead's personal story doesn't advance  much through most of the films in the  series  he shows up for a few minutes and  generally leaves with a few new  cenobytes  but the 10th film in the series 2018's  hellraiser judgment  found pinhead tied up in a cosmic battle  revealing that god and the cenobites  have different plans for serial killers  hell would like to claim them for their  own  but heaven wants to let some run free to  instill godly fear in people  pinhead interferes with the plans of god  and kills an angel sent to negotiate  because of pinhead's actions a serial  murderer is killed in defiance of god's  plan  probably should not have done that  consumed with wrath  god punishes pinhead in the only way he  can because pinhead  is at his core a seeker of pain and a  leader in hell  god takes all that away from him by  making him a mortal man  putting him back on earth and forcing  him to live without his constant  tortures  is the cruelest thing one could do to  the monster and that's exactly how  hellraiser judgment  leaves him just a regular guy again what  could be crueler  but that's not the end of pinhead's  story hellraiser bloodline the fourth  film in the series had already taken a  giant leap forward into the year 2127  where pinhead again has returned to his  full glory  and has attempted to create an  unsealable gateway to hell  cenobites would no longer have to rely  on puzzle boxes to return to earth  at the same time a distant ancestor of  the original creator of the lament  configuration  an engineer named paul merchant no doubt  an amplification of philip le marchant  wants to undo the wrongdoings of his  family and devises a machine called the  elysium configuration  which would destroy all portals to hell  permanently  luring all of the cenobites to a space  station called the minos  merchant activates the device which is  actually the entire space station  the giant machine folds itself into a  massive box of mirrors and perpetual  light  destroying pinhead and the cenobites  forever  what happened in the century between  hellraiser judgment and the year 2127  we'll just have to wait and find out  check out one of our newest videos right  here  plus even more looper videos about your  favorite horror movies are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

